      "short": "$16,9,7,2,14,11,5,4,12,13,3,6,10,15,1,8,17$.\n\nEvery adjacent sum is $9$, $16$ or $25$.",
      "worked": "One arrangement is\n$$16,9,7,2,14,11,5,4,12,13,3,6,10,15,1,8,17.$$\nThe adjacent sums, in order, are\n$$25,16,9,16,25,16,9,16,25,16,9,16,25,16,9,25.$$\nThese are all perfect squares, and each integer from $1$ to $17$ appears exactly once.",
